nd separators are hidden from screen readers. The ellipsis is a button labelled "Show hidden paths" by default; Arrow Down or a keyboard activation opens the dropdown and moves focus to the first hidden link, and it closes on Escape, an outside click or when focus leaves. Items that are leaving are made inert and hidden from assistive technology during their exit. With reduced motion enabled, items fade without sliding and layout movement is turned off.FAQHow do I make breadcrumbs in React?Wrap a BreadcrumbList in Breadcrumb and add a keyed BreadcrumbItem per path segment, with a BreadcrumbLink for ancestors and BreadcrumbPage for the current page. Put a BreadcrumbSeparator inside each item after the first.How do I collapse long breadcrumb trails?Set maxItems on BreadcrumbList. When there are more items, the middle ones move into a BreadcrumbEllipsis dropdown. The minimum is 3, and Infinity turns collapsing off.Does it work with Next.js links?Yes. Pass a render function to BreadcrumbLink that spreads its props onto your router's Link, for example the Next.js Link component.Updated Oct 23, 2026WebWebReact NativeReact NativebeUIProLimited Offer300+ blocks and premium motion components for React and Next.js.$179 lifetime accessExplore beUI ProSponsorsDiamondTracwellVisitor insights for growthIllosAnimated illustrations for product sitesBecome a sponsor
